Arsenal: 
	objdump -d ./arsenal | grep -B2 "ret" | grep -A1 "syscall"
	This is a two-stage pipe to find syscall instructions that are near a ret:

		objdump -d disassembles the whole binary
		grep -B2 "ret" keeps every line containing ret, plus the 2 lines before it (-B2 = before)
		grep -A1 "syscall" from those results, keeps every line containing syscall plus the 1 line after it (-A1 = after

